 And we have like four different seed mixes that we're testing because a lot of this stuff is like not irrigated, right?

01:32:30.000 --> 01:32:34.000
 So, we're trying some pollinator seed mixes.

01:32:34.000 --> 01:32:35.000
 The other thing-

01:32:35.000 --> 01:32:41.000
 Todd has like four different seed mixes that we've implemented on a couple of our detention ponds.

01:32:41.000 --> 01:32:42.000
 To see what works.

01:32:42.000 --> 01:32:43.000
 We have some city hall, obviously.

01:32:43.000 --> 01:32:46.000
 When you walk in, you can see the pollinators that he's done.

01:32:46.000 --> 01:32:49.000
 The pollinators have done outstanding.

01:32:49.000 --> 01:32:50.000
 So, communication is that.

01:32:50.000 --> 01:32:52.000
 Trying to establish some short native grasses.

01:32:52.000 --> 01:32:59.000
 And I think we are tending to, but we're at the beginning stages of trying to see what works as well.

01:32:59.000 --> 01:33:04.000
 But I think that that needs to be communicated, Zach, because what we're hearing from residents is you're doing nothing.

01:33:04.000 --> 01:33:05.000
 And that's not true.

01:33:05.000 --> 01:33:07.000
 That's not what we're hearing.

01:33:07.000 --> 01:33:08.000
 Yeah.

01:33:08.000 --> 01:33:22.000
 But we're not getting that message out where they recognize that, look, we've tackled four different areas in the city with different seed mixes that we're looking to test in an effort to decide which areas in the city are going to do best with this type of re-vegetation.

01:33:22.000 --> 01:33:24.000
 Which areas are we going to leave alone?

01:33:24.000 --> 01:33:25.000
 Which areas are we going to improve?

01:33:25.000 --> 01:33:28.000
 Which areas are we going to come in and knock it down?

01:33:28.000 --> 01:33:31.000
 I don't think that's being communicated effectively.

01:33:31.000 --> 01:33:34.000
 I mean, I'm glad to hear that.

01:33:34.000 --> 01:33:37.000
 That's kind of, for me, that's weird news.

01:33:37.000 --> 01:33:39.000
 That's what I'm going to say.

01:33:39.000 --> 01:33:41.000
 We just need to toot our horn more, you guys.

01:33:41.000 --> 01:33:43.000
 You guys are doing wonderful things.

01:33:43.000 --> 01:33:51.000
 I hope this doesn't feel like, at least from my perspective, this isn't that I'm frustrated, I'm going to beat up on the guys who are doing all the heavy lifting.

01:33:51.000 --> 01:33:52.000
 That's not it at all.

01:33:52.000 --> 01:33:53.000
 I'm grateful.

01:33:53.000 --> 01:34:12.000
 But I don't think that we, as council members, because we're lacking data to share, number one, or as an organization, are doing the best job that we can in communicating these things to the residents so that they see that we're actively pursuing some solutions to some of the problems.

01:34:12.000 --> 01:34:14.000
 But then here's the thing that happens with them.

01:34:14.000 --> 01:34:25.000
 If they don't think that we're addressing the problems, then what they end up doing is when we do community outreach things, when Tyler sends something out, Brandon sends something out for the general plan for downtown.

01:34:25.000 --> 01:34:29.000
 What we're hearing is, why are we spending more money on these things when we can't even address these things?

01:34:29.000 --> 01:34:30.000
 Yep.

01:34:31.000 --> 01:34:38.000
 For a public relations thing, we need to let them know we are addressing those things.

01:34:38.000 --> 01:34:41.000
 The money that you're being taxed for is being spent on your behalf.

01:34:41.000 --> 01:34:42.000
 And we're doing it in these ways.

01:34:42.000 --> 01:34:55.000
 And by the way, we recognize that this is an insurmountable task, and so we're going to elevate it by doing these things that, you know, Steve has talked about in activating, adding more people to the department.

01:34:55.000 --> 01:35:00.000
 And we're going to put a plan in place to bring volunteers, and our 2025 plan is going to be more robust.

01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:01.000
 We hear you.

01:35:01.000 --> 01:35:13.000
 This is the things that we're doing, so that the other things that we reach out to from our departments can have the benefit of good community input that is not always just raging against the machine all the time.

01:35:13.000 --> 01:35:18.000
 So, okay, so I think we heard loud and clear.

01:35:18.000 --> 01:35:25.000
 We need to communicate better with our residents of some of the efforts we're making after we hear complaints or know about that.

01:35:25.000 --> 01:35:30.000
 Look, and I teach Tyler for not getting the word out, but listen, he can't get the word out if he doesn't know.

01:35:30.000 --> 01:35:35.000
 If we didn't know, if it's the department heads that didn't tell him they did for us, how could he get the word out?

01:35:35.000 --> 01:35:41.000
 So we need to internally be able to say, hey, by the way, this is what's going on.

01:35:41.000 --> 01:35:42.000
 It's a big win.

01:35:42.000 --> 01:35:43.000
 Yes.

01:35:43.000 --> 01:35:44.000
 Yeah.

01:35:44.000 --> 01:35:45.000
 We all are too humble.

01:35:45.000 --> 01:35:46.000
 Big win Wednesday.

