06:51:28.660 --> 06:51:37.660
 If we tell the shopping habits, we know sources of entertainment, methods of social interaction, all these things have changed quite considerably, especially with COVID-19.

06:51:37.660 --> 06:51:44.660
 Some things have changed back the same way before, and other things have changed even more a different way.

06:51:44.660 --> 06:51:55.660
 You know, COVID-19, for example, caused people to try a lot more of the grocery delivery and try a lot more of the Uber Eats and all that kind of stuff like that,

06:51:55.660 --> 06:52:00.660
 where that trend is now changing the opposite direction because people can't afford grocery delivery.

06:52:00.660 --> 06:52:02.660
 They can't afford Uber Eats and all that kind of stuff, right?

06:52:02.660 --> 06:52:04.660
 So a lot of things keep changing.

06:52:04.660 --> 06:52:14.660
 And it is making retail, from those I've talked with and the data I've seen, it's making them nervous to act because things are moving so fast,

06:52:14.660 --> 06:52:17.660
 especially when you're talking about building a new brick and mortar business.

06:52:17.660 --> 06:52:24.660
 They hesitate to create that new business, especially in a new market, because they're not really sure how things are going to change.

06:52:24.660 --> 06:52:26.660
 in the next two years.

06:52:26.660 --> 06:52:32.660
 So hopefully as we continue to implement the strategies, we can kind of get them past that.

